{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1533912-ascension-truce","id":1533912,"title":"Ascension Truce","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-04-09T17:16:02-07:00","id":1533912,"title":"Ascension Truce","content":"So,you might have noticed that since the Technocracy reloaded Kickstarter and Book of the Fallen was released ,there have been some metaplot options in recent m20 books about a Truce between the Technocracy and the Traditions<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25411_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25411\" data-vbnamecard=\"25411\">TravisLegge</a> calls it the &quot;Ascension Truce&quot;<br /> The basic idea is simple, it's a Metaplot Option in which the Technocracy and the Traditions decide they should stop fighting each other and focus on solving the REAL problems plaguing humanity, and the REAL enemy of everyone, which of course, is the Nephandi.<br /> I personally love the idea.<br /> i wanted to hear you all's opinion of it though, do you like it? is it something that fits the settings as you run it?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-09T20:17:01-07:00","id":1533927,"title":"","content":"I like it, but not as the default. Players got to earn that alliance through roleplaying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5286-becksworth","name":"Becksworth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-09T21:43:56-07:00","id":1533933,"title":"","content":"Yeah that makes sense","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T02:14:42-07:00","id":1533944,"title":"","content":"Eh in our rounds it is default but only because actually both the upper echelons of Technocracy and Traditions are puppets of the Nephandi so the Nephandi here work like Darth Sidious trying to helplessly corrupt both of them to the core while letting them hunt strawmen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T05:43:12-07:00","id":1533956,"title":"","content":"I don't like it. I get why it's a necessary design choice if your players want to go mixed-faction, but from a setting perspective I don't like it. The kind of evil the Nephandi represent is actually a pretty insignificant force in the world--most people who do evil aren't doing it out of some deliberate all-encompassing malice--and they don't read like actually competent villains. They're a bunch of backstabbing self-absorbed dweebs with no ability to actually appeal to people. So it simply doesn't make any sense for the Nephandi to be the true big bad guys.<br /> <br /> Even if you take out the Nephandi--it seems crystal clear from reading the newer Technocracy books that even their more liberal factions have simply swapped out physical genocide for cultural genocide through assimilation. Admitting to the existence of &quot;reality deviants,&quot; bringing the Bygones back, admitting spirits are spirits, or trying to make the Consensus accommodate the paradigms of the Traditions and Crafts isn't actually on the table. The Technocracy just created a DEI program and tried to rebrand itself as eco-friendly and is trying to get the Traditions to adopt its paradigm that way. And of course the Technocracy <i>would</i> try this (and go back to physical genocide the moment it became more convenient), but most mystic mages should see right through them. This truce is something that would only happen if the Technocracy has such an overwhelming advantage that their enemies need any reprieve, but they aren't quite powerful enough to destroy their enemies without incurring major costs.<br /> <br /> This is consistent with the setting, sure, but the books don't really seem to recognize the nature of the scenario they created. The answer to &quot;Is the Technocracy the baddies&quot; is still <i>very much</i> yes even in their friendlier incarnation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T06:17:35-07:00","id":1533957,"title":"","content":"For clarification, while the Nephandi are a big threat in the Unlikely Allies scenario (a.k.a. &quot;Ascension Truce&quot;) They're not the main driver. The main idea is the Technocracy (and to a lesser degree, the Traditions) have recognized the various Pandora's Boxes they've opened throughout the Ascension war and realize that humanity is on a course to extinction as a result. Both sides have realized they need to set aside their differences (as much as they can, which, mind you, isn't much) to combat the extremes of human ignorance and &quot;misuse&quot; of the tools they feel they've given humanity.<br /> <br /> Is it unlikely? yes.<br /> <br /> Is it a thing that if you want to include in your games *should* take a ton of work for your players to attain and maintain? yes.<br /> <br /> Is it another example of<i><b> massive hubris</b></i> on the part of mages? Also yes.<br /> <br /> They're basically claiming credit for humanity's ability to wreck the planet and each other while assuming the position that their own &quot;enlightenment&quot; (lowercase) is key to averting Armageddon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T06:53:53-07:00","id":1533963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TravisLegge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1533912-ascension-truce?p=1533957#post1533957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For clarification, while the Nephandi are a big threat in the Unlikely Allies scenario (a.k.a. &quot;Ascension Truce&quot;) They're not the main driver. The main idea is the Technocracy (and to a lesser degree, the Traditions) have recognized the various Pandora's Boxes they've opened throughout the Ascension war and realize that humanity is on a course to extinction as a result. Both sides have realized they need to set aside their differences (as much as they can, which, mind you, isn't much) to combat the extremes of human ignorance and &quot;misuse&quot; of the tools they feel they've given humanity.<br /> <br /> Is it unlikely? yes.<br /> <br /> Is it a thing that if you want to include in your games *should* take a ton of work for your players to attain and maintain? yes.<br /> <br /> Is it another example of<i><b> massive hubris</b></i> on the part of mages? Also yes.<br /> <br /> They're basically claiming credit for humanity's ability to wreck the planet and each other while assuming the position that their own &quot;enlightenment&quot; (lowercase) is key to averting Armageddon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the clarification!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T06:55:25-07:00","id":1533964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Citrakayah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1533912-ascension-truce?p=1533956#post1533956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like it. I get why it's a necessary design choice if your players want to go mixed-faction, but from a setting perspective I don't like it. The kind of evil the Nephandi represent is actually a pretty insignificant force in the world--most people who do evil aren't doing it out of some deliberate all-encompassing malice--and they don't read like actually competent villains. They're a bunch of backstabbing self-absorbed dweebs with no ability to actually appeal to people. So it simply doesn't make any sense for the Nephandi to be the true big bad guys.<br /> <br /> Even if you take out the Nephandi--it seems crystal clear from reading the newer Technocracy books that even their more liberal factions have simply swapped out physical genocide for cultural genocide through assimilation. Admitting to the existence of &quot;reality deviants,&quot; bringing the Bygones back, admitting spirits are spirits, or trying to make the Consensus accommodate the paradigms of the Traditions and Crafts isn't actually on the table. The Technocracy just created a DEI program and tried to rebrand itself as eco-friendly and is trying to get the Traditions to adopt its paradigm that way. And of course the Technocracy <i>would</i> try this (and go back to physical genocide the moment it became more convenient), but most mystic mages should see right through them. This truce is something that would only happen if the Technocracy has such an overwhelming advantage that their enemies need any reprieve, but they aren't quite powerful enough to destroy their enemies without incurring major costs.<br /> <br /> This is consistent with the setting, sure, but the books don't really seem to recognize the nature of the scenario they created. The answer to &quot;Is the Technocracy the baddies&quot; is still <i>very much</i> yes even in their friendlier incarnation.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bA very fair take on things,I can see lots of people agreeing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T08:22:33-07:00","id":1533974,"title":"","content":"You can arrive at truce-like conditions a number of ways.<br /> <br /> There's cold war conditions where the struggle is ongoing but there's a pressing need to keep it from overflowing into a hot war. <br /> <br /> There's actual cease fire and/or temporary alliances to face a bigger threat together.<br /> <br /> There's the functional truces that happen between local cells when their nearby opponents are closer than their far away superiors.<br /> <br /> There's the functional truces when there aren't actually enough resources or mages to keep the war going in a hot form so the ideals of the struggle are usually lost among practical concerns. (&quot;yeah we're technically supposed to wipe out witches, but the nearest med center is in the next city and she's here now. It'll be fine.&quot;)<br /> <br /> There's a third kind of functional truce where the political struggles within the Traditions and Technocracy are considered as important as the ideological struggles between the two. This doesn't have to be full civil war level arguments, just a reasonable belief that the direction of your faction is at least as important as the fight against the opponent.<br /> <br /> There's actual ideological drift where the newest generation of the Technocracy sees the struggle against the Traditions as a distraction from their actual goals.<br /> <br /> There's the really depressing corrupt truce where the upper echelons of the Technocracy and Traditions realize they need each other to continue existing in their current form and would rather perpetuate the Ascension War than make strides towards their actual goals.<br /> <br /> The list goes on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-16T08:54:04-07:00","id":1534296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1533912-ascension-truce?p=1533974#post1533974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's actual ideological drift where the newest generation of the Technocracy sees the struggle against the Traditions as a distraction from their actual goals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've run games where there were localized cease-fires between the Traditions and Technocracy due to specific events (like dealing with vampires post-Ravnos incident).This example of yours is probably one I would use for later Ascension games.<br /> <br /> In this case, the Technocracy already &quot;won&quot; the War for Ascension and the Traditions have &quot;lost.&quot; So many younger Technocracy members see little reason to focus much on the Traditions. If Tradition Mages are causing problems, then sure go take them out, but many Technocrats feel that there are much bigger fish to go after these days. So while there isn't an &quot;official&quot; truce, at the ground level you'll see lower rung members of the Technocracy working with Tradition mages to overcome problems facing both factions. The higher ups in the Technocracy don't like this, as they still tend to view the Traditions as their primary threat, but the reality on the ground is quite different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-24T17:48:33-07:00","id":1534667,"title":"","content":"Another thing about Tradition Technocracy Truce, maybe the whole SI is the product of this.<br /> I remind you that the SI thinks that with Vienna they have taken out the global headquarter of the vampiric organization aka Camerilla. Well we know from the one Splat Book that whas a Tremere Hermes Crossover, that thanks to the order of Hermes the traditions think that the Tremere are the leaders of the vampiric union because they where mages before. So maybe thanks to Camerilla pointing at the Sabbat and so showing the Technocracy how big in reality deviant the problem of the vampires is actually, they felt a need to take them out and the tradition used their knowledge to barter with the Technocracy as now both are on their way to make vampires go extinct.<br /> Now being Frenemies the Technocracy still tries to keep informational superiority while the Traditions now try during the hunt to change consensus to make people more open to supernaturality or at least more adverse to technological breakthroughs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-26T03:21:33-07:00","id":1534756,"title":"","content":"I enjoy considering a version of the post-Avatar Storm &quot;truce&quot;, wherein the war got cold because both sides lost access to large amounts of resources and, more importantly, Masters behind the &quot;screaming shards of glass&quot; curtain. They can't prosecute their conflict, and indeed had their respective &quot;chains of command&quot; (such as existed) decapitated, and their networks thrown into disarray. Ironically, this was more a problem for the Technocracy than the Traditions, the latter being used to working autonomously.<br /> <br /> When the Technocracy declared they &quot;won&quot; the Ascension War, it was basically one part of the scattered Union forces declaring it on their own. Trying to bluff the Traditions into backing down, by making the Union seem stronger and, well, more <i>unified</i> than it really was. In truth, between Constructs being cut off from Control and lingering fears about the SPD/Deviant Infiltrators, thousands of Technocrat outposts were left paranoid of each other. Was the loss of Control an attempted coup? Who is in on it? Can those guys over in that other office be trusted?<br /> <br /> While these individual Constructs needed to go along with the bluff, lest the Traditions (or other World of Darkness factions) realize how vulnerable they were, they couldn't fully trust one another. Beginning a years-long process of forming alliances, spying, and other Cold War style activity. Just to reestablish a measure of, well, Control. (It didn't help that the Void Engineers seemed to always drag their feet about trying to &quot;solve&quot; the Avatar Storm. What could those guys be up to? What are they afraid of?).<br /> <br /> All pointing to a persistent ceasefire, where neither side wants to return to open war. Sure, they'll make attacks of opportunity or engage in local conflicts. But all are too wary of escalating too much. They'll even engage in secret - or not so secret - collaboration. A given Union Construct can't necessarily trust the Construct the next city over. But they can always trust a Reality Deviant to be a Reality Deviant. Sometimes, that certainty makes them better allies of convenience.<br /> <br /> Over time, and without the constant attention of Control/the Council (made up of ancient Mages who remember and hold grudges over the Old Days), both sides start to get used to the idea of seeing the other as the &quot;Distinguished Competition&quot;. You don't necessarily like them, and you definitely disagree over the way Reality should be, but they're not necessarily an <i>enemy</i>. Not in the way a Vampire or a Nephandus or even just the systems of mortal society are.<br /> <br /> (I also like the idea that because the Technocracy's reach has been reduced, their ability to guide the systems of Imperialism and Capital towards what they see as their &quot;ideal&quot; forms is reduced. Hence, why all pretense of those systems serving Sleepers has eroded, and Fascism is on the rise. All the guardrails against the abuses of the powerful and their systems have fallen away. Corporate and state actors give in to their worst impulses, regardless of how it threatens the stability of their systems, or the very world itself. The Technocrats on the ground are trying to act as the ultimate Liberal Reformists, trying to save the systems they believe in, while the Traditions are trying to tear them down and replace them.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}